    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** headlining the offense, boasting a standout 74.86 efficiency score. While he faces a neutral park factor, the combination of his elevated position in the order and a favorable 4.27 xERA matchup against Peralta makes him our primary anchor. Similarly, **Jacob Wilson** benefits significantly from a soft matchup against Bradford (5.29 xERA) and a favorable park environment, driving his score to 71.63. We are also monitoring **Jackson Merrill** (69.72), who remains a critical start; his ability to exploit the dynamic platoon advantage against Bibee provides the high-ceiling production required to chase stolen bases and maintain scoring consistency.\n\nStrategic benching remains a focal point as we navigate the daily game caps. **Coby Mayo** was the hardest omission, landing just below the threshold with a 42.34 score. While his profile is intriguing, the optimizer favored the higher projected efficiency and immediate order context of **Dominic Smith** and **Miguel Vargas**. We are exercising caution with **Kyle Tucker** (51.57); despite his pedigree, the tough matchup against Logan Henderson (2.84 xERA) tempers our expectations, relegating him to the utility spot rather than a primary outfield role. We continue to manage the roster without the services of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, who remains on the IL, while **Wade Meckler** and **Nasim Nunez** are held in reserve due to lineup uncertainty and overall projected efficiency trailing our current starters. \n\nThe primary risk today involves the top of the rotation for our opponents. We are bracing for a difficult outing for **Andy Pages** and **Kyle Tucker**, as both must contend with Logan Henderson, whose 2.84 xERA presents a significant hurdle. Furthermore, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Heliot Ramos** benefit from park factors against Cease, the elite skill of that opposing arm necessitates a conservative outlook. Owners should track lineup confirmations closely, as any late-scratch volatility could impact the efficiency of **Drake Baldwin** and **Sam Antonacci** at the top of the order.",
